# The files block_scan_count_rows_utf8_w1, w3 and w8 have 200 rows of one, three and eight columns, where the block
# scan skips the first value of a row at the row end, by itself and with the run call: an invalid first value at rows
# 9 and 150, a quoted one at row 17, an invalid byte in the last column at row 21, a valid non ASCII first value at
# row 25. Each is counted with a comma or a two byte delimiter, without and with a comment byte, which selects the
# four instantiations of the block scan; w8_comment also holds two comment lines. A scan that reads the second
# column validates neither the first nor the last one and returns all 200 rows.

# 1 column, a comma, strict
statement error
SELECT count(*) FROM read_csv('{DATA_DIR}/csv/block_scan_count_rows_utf8_w1.csv', delim=',', new_line='\n', quote='"', escape='"', header=false, auto_detect=false, columns={'a':'VARCHAR'})
